Z||000001||WampusCat||11-29-2001||09:22 AM||||Studied Ngor Chor(5 ancestors) in the 80's.  Currently doing a little Wing Chun when I can fit it in.  No martial arts instructors in SoCal?  Hard to believe, but I know how frustrating it can be trying to find a GOOD instructor.  Especially in some of the places I've lived in the last few years.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Red2m4||11-29-2001||11:39 AM||||Why Wushu?  If you cant find a good wushu school I'm sure there are a LOT of other styles you could learn in Cali.  <P>Best advice I can give is to go watch a few classes, see how the instructors treat the "less than talented" members of the class.  Find one that treats all the students fairly.  <P>I studied Isshin-Ryu karate for a number of years, even ran a school for about a year.  I would recomend any Okinawan (sp?) styles.||||reg||1
